ng"}],"name":"ParkingActivities","purpose":"Retained activity events used by the administrator activity list and report audit trail.","uniques":[]}]},"newDependencies":[],"options":[{"id":"OPT-1","simplest":true,"summary":"Use convention-discovered endpoint modules and EF entity configurations, with Program.cs/AppDb.cs as the one-time composition point and each later feature adding its own wired module and entities. (simplest)","tradeoffs":"Adds a small reflection/discovery convention up front, but lets each vertical slice own its routes and table configuration without shared-file scope overlap or delayed route wiring."},{"id":"OPT-2","simplest":false,"summary":"Use a central explicit route manifest and a central explicit entity registry, updated as each feature is added.","tradeoffs":"The route and schema registration is more visible and type-safe, but every later feature would need to edit shared startup/context files; that conflicts with non-overlapping task scopes and makes later criteria depend on shared-file changes."}],"protectedPathsDeclared":[],"stubs":[{"content":"using System.Threading;\nusing System.Threading.Tasks;\n\nnamespace App.Api.Auth;\n\npublic interface IGoogleIdentityTokenVerifier\n{\n    Task<(string Email, string Name)?> VerifyAsync(string googleIdentityToken, CancellationToken cancellationToken);\n}\n","path":"App.Api/Auth/IGoogleIdentityTokenVerifier.cs","reason":"Tests need to replace the external Google identity verifier with a stand-in before the implementation exists."}],"tasks":[{"approach":"Update Program.cs to register PostgreSQL entity configuration discovery, authentication/authorization, OpenAPI metadata, and startup discovery of every IEndpointModule in the assembly; preserve the existing health route and Swagger/OpenAPI setup. Implement the session, profile, and vehicle operations together with Employee, Vehicle, and Session configurations, the Google verifier seam and implementation, and contract-shaped errors. Keep implementations behind the module convention so later tasks add routes without changing startup.","complexity":"external-dependency","conventions":["Use the existing .NET 9 minimal API, EF Core, PostgreSQL, and EnsureCreated startup conventions.","Keep route modules and entity/configuration classes internal; use the endpoint-module convention and EF configuration discovery established here for later slices.","Use the verifier seam as the only Google identity-system call; register its real HttpClient implementation and read GoogleIdentity:TokenInfoUrl and GoogleIdentity:Audience from appsettings.json, declaring both settings with empty values.","Hash opaque session tokens before persistence; use common ApiError responses for authentication and validation failures.","The API contract is locked: do not edit contracts/openapi.yaml."],"dependsOn":[],"exemplars":["App.Api/Program.cs","App.Api/AppDb.cs"],"fileScope":["App.Api/Program.cs","App.Api/AppDb.cs","App.Api/EndpointModules/IEndpointModule.cs","App.Api/Auth/IGoogleIdentityTokenVerifier.cs","App.Api/Auth/GoogleIdentityTokenVerifier.cs","App.Api/Auth/SessionAuthenticationHandler.cs","App.Api/Auth/ApiErrors.cs","App.Api/Auth/SessionEndpoints.cs","App.Api/Domain/Employee.cs","App.Api/Domain/Vehicle.cs","App.Api/Domain/Session.cs","App.Api/appsettings.json"],"id":"TASK-1","plannedLoc":800,"reqs":["REQ-1: Implement POST /auth/sessions, GET /me/profile, GET and POST /me/vehicles with contract fields, security, statuses, and ApiError behavior; this task owns the first wired routes and the startup/router composition.","Establish assembly-discovered endpoint-module registration and assembly-discovered EF entity configurations so later slices can add their own routes and tables without editing Program.cs or AppDb.cs.","Implement Google Workspace identity verification through the registered IGoogleIdentityTokenVerifier seam; require valid Folio3 identities and persist opaque bearer sessions in PostgreSQL."],"title":"Authenticate employees and expose profile and vehicle routes"},{"approach":"Add the overview endpoint module and the office-clock helper, then introduce OfficeSettings, floor/space capacity records, and dedicated-space assignments with their EF configurations. Ensure a fresh database has the contract-example singleton office settings independently of demo seeding. Return the authenticated employee’s assignment, current office-local status, active vehicle, configured release time, working days, and current availability count.","complexity":"standard","conventions":["Implement routes as an IEndpointModule discovered by the startup convention; do not edit Program.cs or AppDb.cs.","Put each entity's EF configuration beside that entity and map explicit table/column names consistent with the approved data model.","Use the configured office timezone for office dates and preserve Asia/Karachi, 08:00, a 30-day window, Monday-Friday, and holidaysAreWorkingDays=true as initial settings.","Keep response field names and nullable fields aligned with the locked contract."],"dependsOn":["TASK-1"],"exemplars":["App.Api/Auth/SessionEndpoints.cs","App.Api/AppDb.cs"],"fileScope":["App.Api/Parking/ParkingOverviewEndpoints.cs","App.Api/Parking/OfficeClock.cs","App.Api/Domain/OfficeSettings.cs","App.Api/Domain/ParkingFloor.cs","App.Api/Domain/ParkingSpace.cs","App.Api/Domain/DedicatedParkingAssignment.cs"],"id":"TASK-2","plannedLoc":400,"reqs":["REQ-2: Implement GET /parking/config and GET /parking/today with office-local dates/times, configured defaults, the ParkingConfig and ParkingHome fields, and required authentication."],"title":"Serve parking configuration and the employee’s parking home"},{"approach":"Implement the five release operations and their release-rule helper in one vertical slice. Persist each release, its scheduled/cancelled audit events, and activity records with entity configurations; derive floor and space fields from the assigned space. Validate dates and ownership against the office-local configuration, and allow cancellation only for an owned, unclaimed scheduled release.","complexity":"rules-or-algorithm","conventions":["Add routes through the discovered module convention; do not modify shared startup, context, or existing endpoint files.","Use persisted release and audit records; append audit/activity events for state changes rather than replacing history.","Use OfficeClock and OfficeSettings for office dates, scheduling-window bounds, and release times.","Enforce one employee release per office date and return 400 for invalid input, 403 for ineligible holders, and 409 for state conflicts using ApiError."],"dependsOn":["TASK-2"],"exemplars":["App.Api/Parking/ParkingOverviewEndpoints.cs","App.Api/Domain/DedicatedParkingAssignment.cs"],"fileScope":["App.Api/Releases/ReleaseEndpoints.cs","App.Api/Releases/ReleaseRules.cs","App.Api/Domain/ParkingRelease.cs","App.Api/Domain/ReleaseAuditEvent.cs","App.Api/Domain/ParkingActivity.cs"],"id":"TASK-3","plannedLoc":600,"reqs":["REQ-3: Implement POST /parking/releases/today, GET and POST /parking/releases, and DELETE /parking/releases/{releaseId}, including dedicated-holder authorization, date/window validation, office-local claimableAt, filters, conflicts, cancellation, and audit events."],"title":"Release dedicated parking spaces and manage saved releases"},{"approach":"Implement availability and all claim routes together with the ParkingClaim entity/configuration. Persist the claim, authorized plate, employee, vehicle, and release relationship; update release state atomically. Compute floor capacities from persisted floor totals and allocated spaces, include the exact contract allocationRule string, and return contract-shaped 401/403/404/409 responses.","complexity":"rules-or-algorithm","conventions":["Add routes through IEndpointModule discovery; leave shared startup, context, and other slices' files unchanged.","Allocate only office-local claimable releases and order by highest free floor capacity, breaking ties by lowest floor code.","Protect allocation with a database transaction and a unique persisted claim-per-release constraint; map a concurrent loser or unavailable allocation to 409.","Return the existing active claim unchanged with 409 for employee cancellation, as required by Phase 1."],"dependsOn":["TASK-3"],"exemplars":["App.Api/Releases/ReleaseEndpoints.cs","App.Api/Domain/ParkingRelease.cs"],"fileScope":["App.Api/Claims/ClaimEndpoints.cs","App.Api/Domain/ParkingClaim.cs"],"id":"TASK-4","plannedLoc":550,"reqs":["REQ-4: Implement GET /parking/availability, POST /parking/claims, GET /parking/claims/today, and POST /parking/claims/{claimId}/cancel with contract responses, non-dedicated eligibility, active-vehicle ownership, allocation ordering, concurrency protection, and Phase 1 cancellation rejection."],"title":"Expose released-space availability and temporary claims"},{"approach":"Implement the three administrator read operations together with the persisted entrance-verification entity/configuration required by the entry-check list. Filter and paginate roster, verification, and activity data using the contract query parameters, and use the shared ApiError and administrator authorization behavior.","complexity":"standard","conventions":["Add routes through module discovery and protect them with the shared administrator authorization policy.","Reuse the employee, vehicle, activity, and office-clock records already introduced; do not duplicate data maintained by those tables.","Store the entrance-check fields needed for later detection and reporting in EntranceVerifications, with optional employee and vehicle relations.","Use query-level filtering and deterministic pagination, and return the contract's exact field names."],"dependsOn":["TASK-1","TASK-3"],"exemplars":["App.Api/Claims/ClaimEndpoints.cs","App.Api/Domain/ParkingActivity.cs"],"fileScope":["App.Api/Admin/AdminReadEndpoints.cs","App.Api/Domain/EntranceVerification.cs"],"id":"TASK-5","plannedLoc":450,"reqs":["REQ-5: Implement GET /admin/roster, GET /admin/entry-checks, and GET /admin/activity with contract filters, pagination, response shapes, and administrator-only access; standard employees receive 403."],"title":"Add administrator roster, entry-check, and activity lists"},{"approach":"Add the weekly report route and calculate weekday statistics and unused lists from the persisted parking and detection records for the selected office-local week. Include the contract-required totals, timezone, generation timestamp, and lists; validate weekStart and enforce administrator-only access.","complexity":"rules-or-algorithm","conventions":["Add the endpoint through IEndpointModule discovery without editing shared files.","Derive reports from persisted releases, claims, assignments, vehicles, and entrance verifications; do not add scheduled email delivery or a custom report-builder feature.","Use OfficeClock and the persisted office timezone for week dates and generatedAt; return the contract's report schema and ApiError for an invalid date.","Keep the utilization calculation deterministic and document its inputs in the implementation."],"dependsOn":["TASK-2","TASK-3","TASK-4","TASK-5"],"exemplars":["App.Api/Admin/AdminReadEndpoints.cs","App.Api/Domain/EntranceVerification.cs"],"fileScope":["App.Api/Admin/UtilizationEndpoints.cs"],"id":"TASK-6","plannedLoc":450,"reqs":["REQ-6: Implement GET /admin/utilization with optional weekStart, office-local report boundaries, released-space and temporary-claim counts, daily and overall utilization, unused dedicated and temporary records, date validation, and administrator authorization."],"title":"Generate weekly utilization reports from retained parking records"},{"approach":"Implement GET and PUT together as one settings slice, using the existing singleton configuration row. Parse and validate request input explicitly so malformed requests return the locked ApiError shape; persist accepted values and calculate schedule fields using the configured office timezone.","complexity":"standard","conventions":["Add routes through module discovery and use the existing OfficeSettings table/configuration from TASK-2.","Read and write settings in PostgreSQL; derive reportSchedule and nextDelivery fields without introducing report-email delivery.","Validate timezone, time, and email recipient values and return contract-shaped errors and response fields."],"dependsOn":["TASK-2"],"exemplars":["App.Api/Admin/AdminReadEndpoints.cs","App.Api/Domain/OfficeSettings.cs"],"fileScope":["App.Api/Admin/OfficeSettingsEndpoints.cs"],"id":"TASK-7","plannedLoc":300,"reqs":["REQ-7: Implement GET and PUT /admin/settings, persist timezone, release time, and report recipients, return scheduling-window and report schedule fields, validate updates, and enforce administrator authorization."],"title":"Allow administrators to read and update office settings"},{"approach":"Implement detection validation, verification decisions, record persistence, and the operation response together. Match active claims and registered permanent-sticker vehicles using the office-local date, append activity, and return 503 with the service_unavailable ApiError on a verification/database-service outage. Annotate every route module with contract request/response/status/security metadata and verify the generated API document contains all 21 operations without changing contracts/openapi.yaml.","complexity":"rules-or-algorithm","conventions":["Add the detection endpoint through IEndpointModule discovery; all database entities and shared startup behavior must already exist in their first-use slices.","Persist original detection time and office-local date/time, verification decision, entry status, plate, and related employee/vehicle when known.","Fail closed: only a matching active temporary authorization may request green activation; non-car, permanent sticker, failed, and unauthorized detections never request it.","Use the exact contract enums, field names, and status codes; preserve the locked OpenAPI file."],"dependsOn":["TASK-1","TASK-2","TASK-3","TASK-4","TASK-5"],"exemplars":["App.Api/Admin/AdminReadEndpoints.cs","App.Api/Domain/EntranceVerification.cs"],"fileScope":["App.Api/Entrance/DetectionEndpoints.cs"],"id":"TASK-8","plannedLoc":500,"reqs":["REQ-8: Implement POST /integrations/entrance/detections with protected access, car/non-car, permanent-sticker, active-claim, and fail-closed outcomes; persist office-local detection and activity records and return 503 ApiError for a verification-service outage.","REQ-9: Complete PostgreSQL persistence and restart-read behavior for employee, vehicle, parking, configuration, entrance, audit, activity, claim, and settings data across the implemented operations.","REQ-14: Expose all 21 locked-contract operations with their paths, methods, request/response/status and security metadata in the API OpenAPI document; do not add product screens or modify the locked contract."],"title":"Process and persist entrance detections; complete contract operation coverage"},{"approach":"Implement the existing public SeedData.Run method to insert fixed contract-example samples only when each sample identifier is absent. Seed related rows in dependency order, ensure PostgreSQL generated-ID sequences remain safe after explicit example IDs, include three rows per repeatable table and one singleton setting row, and preserve existing database contents.","complexity":"standard","conventions":["Keep SeedData.Run idempotent and never update or delete existing rows; seed records in foreign-key dependency order.","Use three sample rows per repeatable table and the single office-settings row; derive business values and recognizable identifiers from contract examples.","Leave demo seeding controlled by the existing Seed:Demo startup setting; do not seed demo records when it is false.","Seed all tables represented in the approved data model, including the records needed for demo collection and report routes."],"dependsOn":["TASK-1","TASK-2","TASK-3","TASK-4","TASK-5","TASK-6","TASK-7","TASK-8"],"exemplars":["App.Api/SeedData.cs","App.Api/Domain/Employee.cs"],"fileScope":["App.Api/SeedData.cs"],"id":"TASK-9","plannedLoc":500,"reqs":["REQ-10: Insert demo samples only when their identifiers are absent; do not overwrite or delete existing data, and insert no demo samples when Seed:Demo is false.","REQ-11: With demo seeding enabled, place at least two contract-example-based rows in each repeatable contract-backed table.","REQ-12: Seed exactly three rows in each repeatable contract-backed table and one row in singleton office settings, using contract-example-based values.","REQ-13: Keep each repeatable table's demo sample count between two and five; a three-row policy satisfies this count interpretation without removing the separate requirements."],"title":"Seed idempotent contract-example demo records"}]}